How to install widget on database
- php bin/console widget:database

How to reload all widget on database
- php bin/console widget:database --update


List of getting Analytical Data Commands:

- "analytics:datas": Executes all commands for obtaining data
- "device:type": Retrieves data on device types
- "geographic:activity": Retrieves data on geographic activities
- "most:read": Retrieves data on the most read items
- "site:performance": Retrieves data on site performance
- "traffic:acquisition": Retrieves data on traffic acquisition
- "visitors:activity": Retrieves data on user activity

How to Create a Widget:

- Create the Widget class in "src/Bundle/DashboardBundle/Widgets" which implements the "WidgetInterface".
- Create its Twig template in vendor/integrated/integrated/src/Bundle/DashboardBundle/Resources/views
- Define the ID, Name, and path to its view
- Connect to the MongoDB database aleaintegrated and create the widget in the "WidgetConfig" table by defining the attributes ID, Name, and Order (the ID and name must be the same as those of the created class)
- Add the widget in "src/Bundle/DashboardBundle/Resources/config/services.xml"
- Clear the cache

How to setup:
.ENV:
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS="/var/www/html/GoogleCredential.json"

You need to create a service account within the Google API Services, and you need to give this account access to the Analytics accounts you want to be able to get data from.
